# JDK 25 — canonical Windows path (this workstation)

When Ezkey or an agent needs **JDK 25** on **this** Windows workstation, use **exactly** this installation. Do not substitute another JDK 25 build, another vendor, or a generic `JAVA_HOME` from PATH discovery.

**Canonical `JAVA_HOME` (Windows):**

`C:\Tools\jdk-25.0.3+9`

**Same path in Git Bash / typical Unix-style form:**

`/c/Tools/jdk-25.0.3+9`

(Trailing slash optional; no space in the path.)

## How this ties to the repo

- [`scripts/build.sh`](../../scripts/build.sh) auto-probes this path (and close variants) when `JAVA_HOME` is unset, then runs the Maven baseline. On macOS it may use `/usr/libexec/java_home -v 25` when available.
- **Validation entrypoint:** always `./scripts/build.sh` from Git Bash — on Windows, Linux, and macOS. Do not use `.cmd` wrappers.
- When an agent shell is **PowerShell**, invoke Git Bash explicitly: `& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc './scripts/build.sh'` (see [`maven-build.mdc`](maven-build.mdc)).
- If validation fails with `release version 25 not supported`, the compiler in use is **not** JDK 25 — set `JAVA_HOME` to the canonical path above (Windows) or install JDK 25 on Linux/macOS and export `JAVA_HOME` before `./scripts/build.sh`.

## Quick check

From Git Bash after exporting `JAVA_HOME`:

```bash
"$JAVA_HOME/bin/java" -version
```

Expect version output that matches **25.0.3** (or the exact Adoptium/Eclipse build under this path on Windows).
